# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deny by default.
#
# This repository is meant to become public. The deployment it describes holds
# receipt photographs, purchase histories, home coordinates, and the household's
# email addresses. None of that may ever be committed. Broad denials come first;
# the only re-inclusions are directories a CI check vouches for. Do not add a
# re-inclusion without adding the check (see .github/workflows/safeguards.yml).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Everything the running system stores or downloads: receipt images, map tiles,
# USDA downloads, imports, backups. Bind-mounted at runtime, never committed.
# Git will not descend into an excluded directory, so nothing below these paths
# can be re-included by a later rule.
/data/
/data.bak-*/
/backups/
/output/

# Reference clones of other open-source projects. Two of them are AGPL-3.0 and
# this project is MIT: their code must never enter this tree, let alone history.
# The named directories are the clones as they sit today at the repo root; the
# `reference/` directory is where CLAUDE.md says they belong.
/reference/
/cookcli/
/grocy/
/kitchenowl/
/mealie/
/paprika-recipes/

# Database files and dumps, wherever they land.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.dump
*.pgdump
*.backup
*.sql.gz

# Receipt photographs and scans. HEIC is the iPhone default and is easy to forget.
# The scanner (tools/scan_pii.py) cannot read pixels, so these are denied outright;
# the test corpus generates its images at test time rather than committing them.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.heic
*.heif
*.webp
*.gif
*.tif
*.tiff
*.bmp
*.pdf

# Spreadsheets, archives, and mail: the shapes real purchase data arrives in, and
# formats the scanner cannot read.
*.csv
*.tsv
*.xls
*.xlsx
*.ods
*.doc
*.docx
*.eml
*.mbox
*.zip
*.7z
*.rar
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz

# Map tiles and OSM extracts: not personal, but hundreds of megabytes.
*.pmtiles
*.mbtiles
*.osm.pbf

# The single re-inclusion. frontend/public/ holds icons the app serves. CI
# refuses any file there larger than 64 KB, which no receipt photograph is.
!frontend/public/**

# The PII scanner's literal denylist is itself a PII file.
tools/denylist.txt

# Local configuration and secrets.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.local.*
*.pem
*.key

# Tool output about the project rather than part of it (gstack reports carry
# screenshots of the running app, which may show real data).
/.gstack/
/.claude/settings.local.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ordinary build and tooling noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
htmlcov/

node_modules/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
frontend/dist/

.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
